+# Phase 2: Install From An Archive
+
+---
+
+## Status
+
+**Current Status:** 🔴 Not Started (0% — 0/3)
+**Started:** {{START_DATE}}
+**Completed:** {{COMPLETION_DATE}}
+**Blocked By:** —
+
+---
+
+## Objective
+
+Install a llama-swap release from an archive already on disk, and say which release a running
+gateway still runs once another one is current.
+
+### Out of Scope
+Archives for another platform than Linux x86_64.
+
+---
+
+## Tasks
+
+### Install
+- [ ] `gateway install --from <ARCHIVE>`: the release installed from a local archive, its digest checked against `--sha256` or the pinned one
+  Proof: tests on the use case and the command line
+- [ ] `gateway install` names the release the running gateway runs when it is not the new current one, with `ai-ctl down` then `ai-ctl up` to switch
+  Proof: tests on the use case
+
+### Documentation
+- [ ] Both in `docs/commands.md` and the README
+  Proof: a reading of both
+
+---
+
+## Technical Details
+
+### Files to Modify
+```
+src/application/gateway.rs, ports.rs, fakes.rs
+src/infrastructure/gateway_store.rs
+src/presentation/cli.rs, gateway.rs
+docs/commands.md, README.md
+```
+
+### Dependencies
+Phase 1's store methods.
+
+### Constraints
+- No digest from the archive's own directory: a checksums file beside it proves nothing.
